 "method_note": "Capture rate = share of references cited by the 15 included reviews + 6 seeds that the 1,550-record query retrieval contains. Denominator restricted to references that pass the same battery-term AND ML-term title gate as the screening pipeline and are dated 2020 or later (the retrieval window); titles and years are taken from the deposited reference metadata where present and otherwise resolved by DOI (cached in raw_cache/). References pre-2020, unresolvable, without DOIs, or failing the title gate are counted separately in the summary blocks. This estimates retrieval recall against a review-curated ground truth, not against the true literature: the denominator is itself a citation-conditioned sample."
